The response of my model to a shorter tidal lag (185 s for 195), T^2 terms from c + a T + b T^2:  mean longitude +0.68334, perigee -0.00991, node +0.00280
T in centuries back from 2000; arcsec.  "matched" = my run carries the same numbers for the Earth's oblateness as the reference (J2E, J2EDOT and, for DE441, J2ET2), so no cube is expected and none is fitted;
"nearly matched" = my constant-oblateness run against DE431, whose oblateness has a steady rate that this run lacks (the pair I first took for matched; the checking reader made the properly matched run, and run_back16.sh repeats it);
otherwise a cube is fitted as well.

